# Site content → content GitHub

## Standing authorization (do not skip)

Edits under `site_*/` / `site_<name>/` **must** be committed to the **content** GitHub repo as part of the same task.

This is **not** covered by “only commit when the user asks” (that rule is for the **app** git repo only). Touching `site_*` **is** the ask to push content. Do **not** end the turn with “sync was disabled / I’ll leave it local / please commit from Cloud Sync” unless every path below failed — and then report it as a **failure**, not as done.

Folders like `site_4geeks-com/` are **gitignored** in the app repo. Local-only YAML/registry edits are wiped by content sync pull. App `git commit` / `git push` does **not** persist them.

## Resolve target (always)

From [`sites.yml`](sites.yml):

- `contentRoot` = that site’s `content_folder` (e.g. `site_4geeks-com`)
- Content GitHub = `github_repo_url` (may redirect; today often `breatheco-de/website-content-folders`)
- Remote paths **keep** the `site_<name>/` prefix (e.g. `site_4geeks-com/component-registry/.../schema.yml`)

## Definition of done (hard gate)

Before any final response on a task that modified `site_*`:

1. List every changed path under `contentRoot`.
2. Push those paths to the content repo (Path A or B below).
3. Hold a real **`commitSha`** and verify the file(s) on remote.
4. Update local sync state so those paths are no longer pending.

**No SHA → task incomplete.** Do not claim the content fix is shipped.

---

## Path A — app sync helpers (preferred)

Run from the **app repo root**. Always load dotenv so `GITHUB_TOKEN` / `GITHUB_SYNC_ENABLED` match `npm run dev` (bare `tsx` without dotenv often false-negatives “sync disabled”).

```ts
// npx tsx <<'TS'  (from website-v3 root)
import { config as loadDotenv } from "dotenv";
loadDotenv({ quiet: true });

import { markFileAsModified, detectPendingChanges, updateFileAfterCommit } from "./server/sync-state.ts";
import { getConflictInfo, commitAndPush, commitSingleFile } from "./server/github.ts";

const contentRoot = "site_4geeks-com"; // from sites.yml
const files = [
  // absolute-from-root paths that you changed, e.g.:
  "site_4geeks-com/component-registry/list_press_mentions/v1.0/schema.yml",
];

for (const f of files) markFileAsModified(f, "agent", undefined, contentRoot);

const conflicts = await getConflictInfo({ contentRoot });
const remoteTouched: string[] = (conflicts as any)?.changedFiles ?? [];
const overlap = files.filter((f) => remoteTouched.includes(f));
if (overlap.length) {
  // pull ONLY overlapping paths (pullSingleFile / sync helpers), re-apply local edits, then continue
  throw new Error(`Resolve overlap before push: ${overlap.join(", ")}`);
}
// Behind on unrelated files is OK — do not abort.

// One file:
const one = await commitSingleFile({
  filePath: files[0],
  message: "Describe why (content-facing)",
  author: "agent",
  contentRoot,
});
// Many files:
const many = await commitAndPush("Describe why (content-facing)", {
  files,
  contentRoot,
  // force: true  // only after intentional conflict resolve
});

const sha = one.commitSha ?? many.commitHash;
if (!sha) throw new Error(`Content push failed: ${one.error ?? many.error}`);
console.log("commitSha", sha);

// If commitAndPush already updated state, skip; after gh/external push use:
// for (const f of files) updateFileAfterCommit(f, sha, contentRoot);

const still = detectPendingChanges(contentRoot).filter((c) => files.includes(c.file));
if (still.length) console.warn("still pending", still);
```

Confirm: `success` / non-empty `commitSha`|`commitHash`. Print the SHA in the final user message.

---

## Path B — `gh` HTTPS fallback (when Path A fails)

Use when Path A returns “sync disabled”, missing token in the agent shell, or `/api/github/commit` is 403 without staff session. Do **not** stop at Path A failure.

```bash
# From anywhere; requires `gh` auth with write access to the content repo
set -e
CONTENT_REPO="breatheco-de/website-content-folders"   # resolve via sites.yml / gh repo view
CONTENT_ROOT="site_4geeks-com"
APP_ROOT="/Users/…/website-v3"                        # this app checkout
REPO_DIR="/tmp/content-push-$$"

# HTTPS clone (SSH often fails in agent environments)
gh repo clone "https://github.com/${CONTENT_REPO}.git" "$REPO_DIR" -- --depth 20 --branch main
# If clone still tries SSH, set insteadOf or use the https URL explicitly as above.

# Copy ONLY the files you changed (keep site_ prefix)
# Example: one schema
mkdir -p "$REPO_DIR/${CONTENT_ROOT}/component-registry/list_press_mentions/v1.0"
cp "$APP_ROOT/${CONTENT_ROOT}/component-registry/list_press_mentions/v1.0/schema.yml" \
   "$REPO_DIR/${CONTENT_ROOT}/component-registry/list_press_mentions/v1.0/schema.yml"

cd "$REPO_DIR"
git add ${CONTENT_ROOT}/…
git -c user.email="agent@4geeks.com" -c user.name="Cursor Agent" commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Describe why (content-facing)

EOF
)"
git push origin HEAD
SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
echo "commitSha $SHA"
```

Then from the **app** root, mark sync state clean:

```ts
import { updateFileAfterCommit } from "./server/sync-state.ts";
const sha = "…paste SHA…";
const contentRoot = "site_4geeks-com";
for (const f of files) updateFileAfterCommit(f, sha, contentRoot);
```

Verify remote, e.g.:

```bash
gh api "repos/${CONTENT_REPO}/commits/${SHA}" --jq '{sha:.sha[0:7], message:.commit.message, files:(.files|length)}'
```

---

## Conflicts

- **Overlap** (remote changed the same path you changed): pull that path, re-apply your edit, then Path A/B again. Use `force` on sync commit **only** after that intentional resolve.
- **Behind on other paths** (blog/landings/etc.): ignore for your push; Path B on top of latest `main` is fine if your files do not overlap.

## Recurring agent mistakes (avoid)

| Mistake | Correct behavior |
|---|---|
| Finish after editing `site_*` only locally | Path A or B → report SHA |
| Treat “ask before commit” as blocking content push | App git = ask; `site_*` = always push |
| Bare `tsx` → “sync disabled” → stop | `loadDotenv()` then retry, or Path B |
| Abort because site is “behind” on unrelated files | Push non-overlapping paths |
| App-repo commit of `site_*` | Useless — gitignored |
| Vague “please commit in Cloud Sync” as success | Failure unless user must unblock auth |

## Redirect tip (blog)

Prefer exact `meta.redirects` for legacy `/us/...` and wrong-category paths so they 301 **once**. Relying only on the global `/us/` regex plus canonical category fix causes a double redirect.

